[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-141624"] :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x+1=(x-1{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =24 \\\\ (x-1{)}^{2}-1 & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $1$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1{)}^{2}-1+1 & =24+1 \\\\ (x-1{)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1{)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-1{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x-1| & =5 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =1-5=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =1+5=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-4{)}^{2}+{6}^{2}=52.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "0a96ede7-1e29-5ba5-996f-f6e89f379a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "96311a34-81d6-569d-9618-25455f56c8e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection/687ba219d8c9b2fa04add76a6cff5858a48aea851ffa07746ca60b9a04b7f2d1" :answer/id #uuid "97a5605b-0ecc-554b-a52a-e3db909c1909" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "109" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" :answer/id #uuid "a3807fac-4bde-54de-b60a-b3a79189d5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" :answer/id #uuid "b6b9a054-fb5f-580c-9c47-155469005945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "104" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "472e978a-a6d3-5c29-aef2-f78889b6b6ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141812/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" :answer-field/choices ["q-141812/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" "q-141812/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" "q-141812/selection/687ba219d8c9b2fa04add76a6cff5858a48aea851ffa07746ca60b9a04b7f2d1" "q-141812/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" "q-141812/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141812" :question/id #uuid "a63dfb9f-93e3-51bc-aa25-108f3448b60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-141812" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}-8x=20.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-8x+16$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x+16=(x-4{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot x & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2}-16 & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $16$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4{)}^{2}-16+16 & =20+16 \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4{)}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-4{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\ |x-4| & =6 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =4-6=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =4+6=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-2{)}^{2}+{10}^{2}=104.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "d6a46742-4b3d-528e-9d92-9ea072ea5aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "0e21f58a-d254-5cd3-bd66-e742cf8b1efa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection/0c91aee12841e83df8a63bea4f335135e4f592b0fef26da9fddc6b9cb7ae4e6d" :answer/id #uuid "1e809ade-4805-5a00-9fc5-fca7f7eb86ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "61" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "a9138edf-cdde-533f-b361-afcdd84e50d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06" :answer/id #uuid "32046602-5391-5b13-882a-762be049064e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "734e5959-1aa6-5bb3-8c05-d82fcd98b000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142011/selection/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06" :answer-field/choices ["q-142011/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-142011/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" "q-142011/selection/0c91aee12841e83df8a63bea4f335135e4f592b0fef26da9fddc6b9cb7ae4e6d" "q-142011/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" "q-142011/selection/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142011" :question/id #uuid "93a225b4-f6a2-5f6f-bfee-a72c21c4b8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-142011" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}-6x=16.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-6x+9$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-6x+9=(x-3{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot x & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-3{)}^{2}-9 & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $9$ to both sides: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3{)}^{2}-9+9 & =16+9 \\\\ (x-3{)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3{)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-3{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x-3| & =5 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =3-5=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3+5=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-2{)}^{2}+{8}^{2}=68.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142011/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142015/selection/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06" :answer/id #uuid "7f8c088