 form $(b+p{)}^{2}=q.$   Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}+14b+14 & =0 \\\\ {b}^{2}+14b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2} & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=7,$ $q=35$ and $p+q=42.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection/3471c7ed513eef9d0cd9059740986fb59ec5061873adf039272ac452fbf2fb6f" :answer/id #uuid "57bca682-aecc-5d9c-bd69-32beda67af72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection/ba4d7ec0a7962cf16a99c3c7ce49572a5da415eca8a72e202364a7e316dc6fe3" :answer/id #uuid "25227fd6-030d-5b70-871b-0be18adda881" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection/cba0513e46ee8106cbb3e4745c9a5aa539d892c3126b2d97e158488a175bac6a" :answer/id #uuid "7808c611-79d3-5d3f-b6d9-fcbbcca2500b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection/5bfb6549629f901efa3f22cef34e183ce5ef91af3f0dc0eac042daeb10443598" :answer/id #uuid "62718a36-e115-5db8-a5a2-ca97b4f0e195" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection/085ac88488a1de05d78693c9a20a5f1a95808ed20fa6a1aab9d3f092f5e4d7f1" :answer/id #uuid "a3f1d611-aac3-5e70-8fa7-6ce43ecb9137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5069923-e6bc-581f-9b55-9d4e811ded5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12995/selection/ba4d7ec0a7962cf16a99c3c7ce49572a5da415eca8a72e202364a7e316dc6fe3" :answer-field/choices ["q-12995/selection/3471c7ed513eef9d0cd9059740986fb59ec5061873adf039272ac452fbf2fb6f" "q-12995/selection/ba4d7ec0a7962cf16a99c3c7ce49572a5da415eca8a72e202364a7e316dc6fe3" "q-12995/selection/cba0513e46ee8106cbb3e4745c9a5aa539d892c3126b2d97e158488a175bac6a" "q-12995/selection/5bfb6549629f901efa3f22cef34e183ce5ef91af3f0dc0eac042daeb10443598" "q-12995/selection/085ac88488a1de05d78693c9a20a5f1a95808ed20fa6a1aab9d3f092f5e4d7f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12995" :question/id #uuid "46e02905-4bf4-54c0-a32f-d28f800b59c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-12995" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The equation ${z}^{2}-25=-10z$ can be written in the form $(z+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-10z$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-25 & =-10z \\\\ {z}^{2}+10z & =25 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z & =25 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=5,q=50,$ and $p+q=55.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112488/selection/cb628a086e207564e983ddfe19b271327679a9db58f917b95f63eafafef7c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "7e040d18-b072-5028-92c0-759a0ebf072a" :answer/type :answer.type/math