le false :question/problem "The equation ${n}^{2}-11=2n$ can be written in the form $(n+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $2n$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-11 & =2n \\\\ {n}^{2}-2n & =11 \\\\ {n}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot n & =11 \\\\ {n}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot n+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11 \\\\ (n-1{)}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1{)}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11 \\\\ (n-1{)}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-1,q=12,$ and $p+q=11.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1{)}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\sqrt{(n-1{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |n-1| & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ n-1 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ n & =1\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112488/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112488"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
